  "description": {
    "raw": "You conjure a herd of aurochs or similar herd animal that\nimmediately stampedes in the direction you indicate. The herd\ntakes up a 20-foot-radius space and moves at a rate of 120\nfeet per round in a straight line. Any creatures caught in the\nherd’s path take 4d6+9 points of damage that round as they\nare trampled beneath dozens of animals’ hooves. A successful\nReflex save halves this damage.\n\nIf the stampede’s path would put it in an obviously\ndangerous area (such as over a cliff or through a fire) or force it\nto move through a solid barrier, the herd stops at the obstacle\nand moves in a new randomly determined direction until it\nreaches another obstacle or the spell’s duration ends.",
    "search_text": "\"you conjure a herd of aurochs or similar herd animal that\\nimmediately stampedes in the direction you indicate. the herd\\ntakes up a 20-foot-radius space and moves at a rate of 120\\nfeet per round in a straight line. any creatures caught in the\\nherd’s path take 4d6+9 points of damage that round as they\\nare trampled beneath dozens of animals’ hooves. a successful\\nreflex save halves this damage.\\n\\nif the stampede’s path would put it in an obviously\\ndangerous area (such as over a cliff or through a fire) or force it\\nto move through a solid barrier, the herd stops at the obstacle\\nand moves in a new randomly determined direction until it\\nreaches another obstacle or the spell’s duration ends.\"",
    "sections": []
